# Component library charter

RosettaDash ships one logical component library across **six consumer targets**:

| Target | Package / surface |
|--------|-------------------|
| Plain HTML/JS/CSS | `@rosettadash/web-components` + copy-paste snippets (see `packages/web-components/.cursor/rules/vanilla-target.mdc`) |
| Web Components | `@rosettadash/web-components` |
| React | `@rosettadash/react` |
| Angular | `@rosettadash/angular` |
| Vue | `@rosettadash/vue` |
| Svelte | `@rosettadash/svelte` |

The Angular **builder** (`apps/client`) is the authoring app — not a consumer runtime. It previews and exports; it does not define the public component contract.

## Source of truth (in order)

1. **`tools/runtime-taxonomy/manifest.mjs`** — which components exist, their subpaths, export names, and generation pattern (`native` | `manual` | `ce-host`).
2. **`@rosettadash/web-components`** — canonical DOM, attributes, events, and styles for every component.
3. **`tools/runtime-taxonomy/*-templates.mjs`** — shared markup/props for codegen into React/Angular/Vue/Svelte.
4. **`@rosettadash/core`** — taxonomy registry, Export IR, shared math (equirect filters, BYOK), validation.
5. **Numbered docs** (`docs/33`–`docs/43`, `docs/28`, `docs/35`) — long-form reference; when a doc disagrees with manifest or code, flag the conflict.

**Never** add a public runtime export without a manifest entry. Framework-only exports are bugs unless listed under Grandfathered debt below.

## Three parity levels

Every manifest component must satisfy all three over time:

| Level | Must match across runtimes |
|-------|------------------------------|
| **API** | Subpath `@rosettadash/<runtime>/<group>/…/<component>`, PascalCase export, prop names, event names, typed `.d.ts` |
| **DOM** | Root BEM block (`rd-*`), `data-testid`, semantic structure, child/slot placement |
| **Behavior** | Interaction, keyboard, empty/loading/error states, teardown on unmount |

API + DOM parity is required before merge. Behavior parity is required before calling a component "done"; stubs are grandfathered only where listed.

## Implementation patterns

| Pattern | When | Canonical layer |
|---------|------|-----------------|
| `native` | Layout, inputs, charts, most atoms | WC `RosettaAtomElement` → codegen per framework |
| `manual` | Media CEs, geo-map, wasm/media | Hand-written WC → thin CE-host in frameworks |
| `ce-host` | Same as manual with `wcImport` | Framework wraps WC custom element |

Heavy logic (equirect math, BYOK crypto) lives in **`@rosettadash/core`**, never duplicated per runtime.

## Add-a-component workflow (mandatory order)

1. Jira ticket + feature branch (see `01-jira-ticket-and-branch.mdc`).
2. Add **`ComponentDefinition`** + palette group (2–7 items) in `packages/core`.
3. Add **`RuntimeAtomEntry`** to `manifest.mjs` with `subpath`, `exportName`, `pattern`, `testId`.
4. Implement **web-components** (native or manual CE).
5. Run codegen: `npm run generate:web-components-runtime` and the target framework script(s).
6. Add **vanilla snippet** to `packages/web-components/README.md` (or dedicated docs section).
7. Add **Storybook** story via `tools/storybook-shared/` (all five `apps/storybook-*`).
8. Update **exporters** for new palette type (all UI exporters or matrix tests fail).
9. Use in a **proof app** screen when the component is user-facing.
10. Run `npm run verify` (and `verify:all` if builder UI changed).

Standalone export must work before package-mode imports (`02-standalone-first-export.mdc`).

## Grandfathered debt (do not extend)

Known gaps vs target parity. **Do not add new entries.** Close with a dedicated parity ticket.

### React-only exports (no manifest entry; missing on Angular/Vue/Svelte/WC)

- `layout/scroll-region`, `layout/filter-grid`, `layout/geo-explorer`, `layout/form-section`
- `visual/chart/sankey`, `visual/chart/venn`
- `visual/destination/destination-select-list`, `visual/filter/filter-summary`
- `visual/display/equirect-globe`
- `visual/media/carousel`, `visual/media/video-metadata`

### React + Angular only (missing Vue/Svelte/WC/manifest)

- `visual/media/equirect-sphere-viewport`, `visual/media/flat-video-viewport`

### Implementation depth stubs (manifest entry exists; behavior incomplete)

- `visual/display/3d-geo-globe` — full Three.js in WC/React/Angular; Svelte/Vue remain codegen stubs

### Tooling gaps

_(None — `generate:svelte-runtime` added to root `package.json`.)_

### Cross-runtime embed exceptions (proof apps only)

- Vue/Svelte proof apps may embed React for Authoring/Globe ahead-of-parity — documented in `docs/43-destination-atlas-proof-apps.md`. Not a license for runtime package skew.

